bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, 0, "form_control_label_width_milli_px, k > 1 branch: resolve_font_metrics_with_language_milli(family, label, num * 1000 * k / den) is called before the FORM_CONTROL_MEASURE_MAX_PX cap that bounds the oversampled k = 1 measurement. A large authored control font at a high device scale (e.g. font-size:200px at k = 4 = 800 px) is measured uncapped; the milli resolver itself falls back to the whole-px path above 512 px and uses a reference size of 8 x px capped at 512, so precision and cost at large sizes are unverified."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, P3, open, "web render: device-scale button label width path skips the FORM_CONTROL_MEASURE_MAX_PX cap", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.spl, 1004, "<button style=font-size:200px>Go</button> at device scale 4; inspect the size passed to resolve_font_metrics_with_language_milli", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 tabbar lane: found in review, not reproduced. Either apply the cap (fall back to the oversampled path above it) or document why the milli resolver's own 512 px limits make it unnecessary."

